1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,873
A saved template changes how your site renders.

2
00:00:03,873 --> 00:00:07,939
The Preview button of the Templates module shows a template on a real

3
00:00:07,939 --> 00:00:09,565
page before you save it.

4
00:00:09,565 --> 00:00:12,980
This video covers using it, how it works, and its limits.

5
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:20,978
A template of the Templates module is matched by name.

6
00:00:20,978 --> 00:00:25,509
Name it after a shape or one of its alternates, such as Content__BlogPost,

7
00:00:25,509 --> 00:00:30,040
and once it is saved it is used instead of a template file with that name.

8
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:34,617
The Preview button renders a page of your site with the template as

9
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:36,189
it stands in the editor.

10
00:00:36,189 --> 00:00:40,750
Nothing is saved, so visitors keep seeing the saved version until you press Save.

11
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:49,999
The Templates page is under Design, Templates in the admin menu, and lists

12
00:00:49,999 --> 00:00:51,763
each template by name.

13
00:00:51,763 --> 00:00:57,370
On this site, Content__BlogPost is the template that draws the page of a blog post.

14
00:00:57,832 --> 00:00:58,874
Let's open it.

15
00:00:58,874 --> 00:01:03,094
The editor has fields for the Name, the Description, and the Content, which

16
00:01:03,094 --> 00:01:04,500
is written in Liquid.

17
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,303
This template puts the words Posted by above the title of the post,

18
00:01:08,303 --> 00:01:11,012
then renders the content of the post below it.

19
00:01:11,493 --> 00:01:15,174
The action bar at the bottom of the page has a Preview button,

20
00:01:15,174 --> 00:01:16,689
after Save and Cancel.

21
00:01:16,689 --> 00:01:20,803
It opens the preview in its own browser tab, so the editor stays open.

22
00:01:21,268 --> 00:01:26,318
The preview tab opens on the home page of your site, which here is the blog.

23
00:01:26,318 --> 00:01:28,659
It lists the posts as summaries.

24
00:01:28,659 --> 00:01:33,524
The theme draws each summary with its own, more specific template, so the

25
00:01:33,524 --> 00:01:37,158
Content__BlogPost template does not change this page.

26
00:01:41,416 --> 00:01:45,179
To try the template on another page, follow a link in the preview.

27
00:01:45,179 --> 00:01:46,800
Let's open the blog post.

28
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:50,876
The saved template renders it, with the words Posted by above the title.

29
00:01:51,338 --> 00:01:55,770
Back in the editor tab, let's finish the byline by typing the editorial

30
00:01:55,770 --> 00:01:57,324
team after Posted by.

31
00:01:57,324 --> 00:02:01,008
Each change goes to the preview tab, and nothing is saved.

32
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:05,823
The preview tab renders the blog post again, with the finished byline.

33
00:02:05,823 --> 00:02:11,250
It remembers the page you opened, and renders that page after every change in the editor.

34
00:02:11,739 --> 00:02:14,197
When the result is right, press Save.

35
00:02:14,197 --> 00:02:17,569
The template is stored, and the Templates list opens.

36
00:02:18,028 --> 00:02:23,212
The preview tab shows Preview Disconnected, because the editor page it followed has gone.

37
00:02:23,212 --> 00:02:27,578
The saved template applies to the site, and you can close the preview tab.

38
00:02:31,778 --> 00:02:36,694
Whenever the content changes, the editor tab stores the name and the content

39
00:02:36,694 --> 00:02:39,032
of the template in local storage.

40
00:02:39,032 --> 00:02:43,588
The preview tab shares that storage, so it is told about every change.

41
00:02:44,338 --> 00:02:48,447
The preview tab posts the name, the content and the page address to

42
00:02:48,447 --> 00:02:51,261
the Render action of the Preview controller.

43
00:02:51,261 --> 00:02:55,708
The action keeps the template in the HTTP context, then builds the Detail

44
00:02:55,708 --> 00:02:57,678
display of that content item.

45
00:02:58,428 --> 00:03:02,687
The PreviewTemplatesProvider reads the template from the HTTP context.

46
00:03:02,687 --> 00:03:08,122
The TemplatesShapeBindingResolver checks it first for every shape, so the template from the

47
00:03:08,122 --> 00:03:11,148
editor wins over a saved one with the same name.

48
00:03:15,348 --> 00:03:17,633
The preview needs two permissions:

49
00:03:17,633 --> 00:03:20,546
Manage templates and Manage Liquid templates.

50
00:03:20,546 --> 00:03:24,088
The Administrator and Editor roles have both by default.

51
00:03:24,838 --> 00:03:28,922
The preview renders the home page when it is a content item, or

52
00:03:28,922 --> 00:03:33,597
any published content item that has an address from the Autoroute module.

53
00:03:33,597 --> 00:03:38,568
For any other address, it shows Preview Error with a status code, such as 404.

54
00:03:39,318 --> 00:03:43,434
A preview template applies to every shape on the page with its name,

55
00:03:43,434 --> 00:03:46,326
unless a more specific template matches first.

56
00:03:46,326 --> 00:03:50,331
To try a template for summaries, open a page that lists them, such

57
00:03:50,331 --> 00:03:52,278
as the home page of the blog.

58
00:03:53,028 --> 00:03:56,201
The Edit Admin Template page has no Preview button.

59
00:03:56,201 --> 00:03:58,928
Admin templates are not previewed this way.

60
00:04:00,928 --> 00:04:04,742
The Preview button renders a page of your site with the template as

61
00:04:04,742 --> 00:04:08,190
typed in the editor, and saves nothing until you press Save.

62
00:04:08,190 --> 00:04:09,548
Thanks for watching.

